<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>

    <!-- THE BROWSER TAB.

         `web.layout` is the <html> skeleton behind every backend page and
         behind the login page, and its head carries:

             <link type="image/x-icon" rel="shortcut icon"
                   t-att-href="x_icon or '/web/static/img/favicon.ico'"/>

         Nothing in this product had ever set `x_icon`, so every tab of every
         client showed Odoo's icon all day. `website` sets it — from
         `website.favicon`, its own record — but only on the FRONTEND, and only
         when `website` is installed. The backend has no such record.

         WHY A VIEW AND NOT A FIELD ON res.company. Because there is no such
         field. `res.company.favicon` does not exist in Odoo 19: `logo`,
         `uses_default_logo`, `primary_color` are on `base`'s res.company, and
         the favicon is on the `website` MODEL. Writing one on install crashed
         the registry with `AttributeError: 'res.company' object has no
         attribute 'favicon'`, which took nine CI jobs down at once — every job
         that installs this module.

         A view is the better answer anyway, and not merely the available one:
         it is loaded by the module's own data file, so it reaches an install
         and an upgrade by the same route, with no post_init_hook, no
         migration, and no company-by-company write that a new tenant could be
         created after.

         `x_icon or` is KEPT, deliberately. Where `website` is installed, that
         variable holds the client's own website favicon — theirs, chosen in
         their own website settings, and never ours to overwrite. Ours is the
         fallback that used to be Odoo's, which is exactly the surface that
         belongs to the product.
    -->

    <template id="favicon" inherit_id="web.layout" name="SapianERP favicon">
        <xpath expr="//link[@rel='shortcut icon']" position="attributes">
            <attribute name="type">image/png</attribute>
            <attribute name="t-att-href">x_icon or '/sapian_theme/static/src/img/favicon.png'</attribute>
        </xpath>
    </template>

</odoo>
